I fixed #1167 and committed it as 63e47415. Build, the full test suite, clippy with -D warnings and the fmt check all pass.

The change: I deleted yoyo's hand-copied list of overflow phrases (OVERFLOW_PHRASES). is_overflow_error now builds an assistant error message from the text and asks yoagent's public Message::is_context_overflow(). That is the same check yoagent runs on the error_message field that prompt.rs reads. So Azure's peak-load rate limit no longer counts as a context overflow, and model_context_window_exceeded now does.

Where I didn't follow the plan: it suggested ProviderError::classify(400, msg). I read that code first, as the plan asked, and it doesn't fit:
• It treats whitespace-only text as an overflow, because of a rule meant for empty HTTP bodies.
• It doesn't recognise the "Context overflow: " prefix, which is how an empty-body 400/413 overflow actually shows up in error_message.

The Message check handles both. As a side effect, empty-body overflows are now caught too; the old list missed them.

Tests: they're in the new src/prompt_retry_overflow_tests.rs, and every expected value comes from calling yoagent rather than from a list I typed:
• Azure's text, copied from yoagent's own test fixture → not an overflow.
• model_context_window_exceeded → overflow.
• The empty-body overflow text → overflow.
• One real overflow message per provider → overflow, matching both of yoagent's checks.
• Near-misses (a rate-limit message, "Request exceeds the maximum allowed size", empty and blank text) → not an overflow.

No existing test changed or failed.

Check that the tests catch the bug: I put the old broad phrase "exceeds the maximum" back in with a NEUTERED marker, counting the marker before running. The Azure test and the near-miss test both failed by name. After restoring, there were 0 markers and all 5 tests passed.

How much this mattered before (from reading yoagent 0.27.7's code, not from a real run): yoagent turns HTTP 429/503/529 into a rate-limit error whose text doesn't include the response body. It also flags Azure's mid-stream payload as a rate limit before checking for overflow. So the Azure text would only have reached yoyo if a provider sent it with some other status code, or in a payload yoagent doesn't recognise as a rate limit. I don't know of any user who actually got compacted because of this.

Other edits: I lowered prompt_retry.rs's registered size in tests/module_size.rs from 2804 to 2800 lines. I also added an ARCHITECTURE.md entry that marks the Day 194 note citing OVERFLOW_PHRASES as superseded.
